Package: linuxcolors
Title: Colour Palettes from the Identity Colours of Linux Distributions
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: 
    person("Ilya", "Kashnitsky", , "ilya.kashnitsky@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Colour palettes built from the brand colours of popular Linux
    distributions (Ubuntu, Arch Linux, Fedora, Debian, Linux Mint, and
    more), designed following best practices for scientific colour use
    (Crameri, Shephard & Heron 2020 <doi:10.1038/s41467-020-19160-7>):
    qualitative palettes optimised for colour-vision deficiency, and
    sequential and diverging palettes with linear, monotonic lightness that
    are perceptually uniform and readable in greyscale. Includes 'ggplot2'
    scales and helpers to extract and preview colours.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
URL: https://github.com/ikashnitsky/linuxcolors
BugReports: https://github.com/ikashnitsky/linuxcolors/issues
